a vigil for british journalists dom  phillips and indigenous expert bruno  pereira  family friends and colleagues of the  pair gathered in rio de janeiro  demanding to know what's happened to  them  they went missing a week ago in the  javari valley an area in the amazon  twice the size of japan and home to the  largest number of uncontacted tribes in  the world  the vigil was held on capacabana beach  the place where phillips used to paddle  surf before moving to northeastern  brazil to write a book about saving the  amazon  he was on his way back from an  expedition with pedera when both men  disappeared  human remains were reportedly found  where the pair was last seen but they  are still being identified  this was dom's last trip there he told  my sister his wife alessandra that he  needed one more interview to finish his  book i think dom went to the amazon  because he belonged there he's an  english man who was born in the wrong  place he loved the rainforest and their  inhabitants  pereira used to work for funai the  government agency responsible for  protecting brazil's indigenous people  bruno was forced to leave the agency  because he did not agree with president  j bolsonaro's policy of opening up the  amazon for commercial exploitation and  leaving it unprotected  there are only 1400 people in our agency  and we have to protect one million  indigenous people occupying an area that  represents 13 percent of brazil's  territory  pereira started working on his own with  the javadi tribes we accompanied him  during an expedition several months ago  in the same area where he was last seen  with dom phillips pereira was already  being threatened because he was helping  local tribes collect evidence of the  invasions to their territories and  report them to local authorities  at first we were very hopeful that both  men were alive because dom was with  bruno who is very experienced the family  thought they must have been ambushed but  managed to hide the boat and escape  through the forest but our week has gone  by and our hopes are diminishing all we  want now is for them to be found we have  a right to know what happened to them  this march is not only to put pressure  on the government to find writer don  phillips and indigenous expert bruno  pereira it's also for a bigger cause  people here say  both men defended saving the amazon  monica yanakiv al jazeera rio de janeiro
 

